Z||000002||Ken Wittlief||07-17-2001||10:46 AM||||hey how are you gonna go about this<P>I was looking at cars all across the US when I bought my '85 SE aout 2 months ago.<P> I was thinking if I could find one in a major city, I could get a discount ticket from JetBlue and fly all the way from NY to CA for less than $200<P> and would take a reasonable sized tool box, couple of days worth the clothes, money orders for the car and travel expenses<P>  and would fly out<P>  inspect and test drive the car<P>  pay for it if I liked it<P>  call my insurance agent back in NY, have him fax me an insurance card<P>  get a temp tag at the state the car was in (about $10)<P>  and drive the car home cross country<P>   in fact I was the high bidder on a sweet little '88 Yellow formula with T tops and great looking allow wheels in CA for $2k on ebay for couple days - but it finally sold for $3000 - and I had already bought my '85se but this one was too good to pass up for $2k - I almost had two - wife woulda killed me!<P>   I was thinking of taking the plates off another car and driving a car home that way - not worth it - way too much risk for the return on investment (save what?! $10 for a temp tag?)<P>  (its too bad I missed out on that yellow formula - driving from CA to NY in the springtime in a T-top Forumula coulda been a SUPER road trip).||||reg||1
